;;; ext-lambda-lists.lisp: lambda lists for the operators of dotcl's own packages
;;;
;;; The DOTCL, DOTNET, DOTCL-MOP and DOTCL-CLTL2 counterpart of
;;; cl-lambda-lists.lisp, read the same way: DOTCL:FUNCTION-LAMBDA-LIST answers
;;; an external symbol of one of these packages listed here, and the function
;;; object it names, with the entry below. Most of these operators are written
;;; in C# and record no lambda list of their own, and the macros made by
;;; registering an expander record the expander's.
;;;
;;; Names follow the docstrings and docs/ (docs/dotnet-package.md for DOTNET),
;;; AMOP for DOTCL-MOP and CLtL2 for DOTCL-CLTL2. Each section is
;;; (PACKAGE-NAME (SYMBOL-NAME "PARAMETERS") ...), with the same rules as the
;;; COMMON-LISP table: no defaults, &BODY and nested lists for macros only,
;;; plain ASCII. A symbol a build leaves out (an emit-only or Windows-only
;;; function) is skipped. test/regression/ext-builtin-lambda-lists.lisp checks
;;; that every fbound external symbol of these packages answers and that each
;;; entry agrees with what the function accepts.

